+      "content": "You know relative clauses with *que* from B1 Unit 5 and the present subjunctive from A2 Unit 27. Now put them together. English uses the same verb in both cases: \"I'm looking for a flat that has a balcony\" can mean any flat at all, or one you already know about. Spanish makes you choose. If you cannot point at the thing, because you are only looking for it, hoping for it or not sure it exists, the verb after *que* goes into the subjunctive. If the thing is real and you know it, the verb stays in the indicative."
